NOTICE — attribution and upstream credits
==========================================

This repository builds heavily on prior open-source reverse-engineering of the
XGecu T76 (and the T48/T56/TL866 family). The Rust port in `minipro-rs/` and the
analysis in `docs/` would not exist without the following work.

Matt Brown (nmatt0) — minipro `t76-improvements` fork
-----------------------------------------------------
    https://gitlab.com/nmatt0/minipro/-/tree/t76-improvements  (GPL-3.0)

The reverse-engineered C drivers for the T48/T56/T76 USB protocols, the T76's
FPGA/bitstream lifecycle, the firmware-update transport, and the `InfoICT76.dll`
field/variant transforms are Matt Brown's work. The C tree vendored here at
`minipro-t76/` is that fork, and the Rust drivers in
`minipro-rs/crates/minipro-proto/` (`t48.rs`, `t56.rs`, `t76.rs`) and the DLL
parser in `minipro-rs/crates/minipro-db/src/dll.rs` are direct ports of it — the
`t*.c` line citations throughout the Rust source point at his code.

radiomanV — Xgecu_T76 — FPGA-side tooling
-----------------------------------------
    https://github.com/radiomanV/Xgecu_T76  (The Unlicense)

FPGA bitstream / uploader tooling and hardware documentation for the T76's
Anlogic FPGA + WCH CH569 MCU.

XGecu / Xgpro
-------------
`InfoICT76.dll` and the `algoT76/*.alg` FPGA bitstreams are XGecu's proprietary
data, redistributed by the community mirror at
https://github.com/Kreeblah/XGecu_Software . They are not part of this project's
source; the tooling here parses/consumes them but does not claim ownership.

